"modules.companion.turnedOn": "Stream overlay turned on.",
"modules.companion.popup": "The game runs on {0}, where companion.html does not exist (or inside a frame), so the companion opens on www.legendmod.ml and only that window gets the data. Another tab or an OBS source can only listen when the game runs on www.legendmod.ml or jimboy3100.github.io in the same browser.",
"modules.companion.blocked": "The browser blocked the window. Allow pop-ups for this site, or open {0} yourself.",
"modules.companion.noBc": "This browser has no BroadcastChannel: only a companion opened with the button gets the data.",
"modules.companion.page.title": "Legend Mod companion",
"modules.companion.page.h1": "Legend Mod companion: stream overlay and second screen",
"modules.companion.page.intro": "Shows your game live: mass, rank, time alive, minimap, leaderboard, events and (optionally) chat. Nothing goes over the network: the game tab sends the data to this page inside your browser.",
"modules.companion.page.step1": "1. Turn it on in the game",
"modules.companion.page.step1Text": "Settings › HUD › <b>Stream overlay / second screen</b> (off by default). <b>Stream overlay: include chat lines</b> adds the chat. The button <b>Open companion</b> under the option opens this page.",
"modules.companion.page.step2": "2. Open this page on the game's own address",
"modules.companion.page.step2a": "The game and this page talk over a <code>BroadcastChannel</code>, which only reaches pages of the <b>same origin in the same browser</b>.",
"modules.companion.page.step2b": "Game on <code>https://www.legendmod.ml/...</code>: open <code>https://www.legendmod.ml/companion.html</code>.",
"modules.companion.page.step2c": "Game on <code>https://jimboy3100.github.io/...</code>: open <code>https://jimboy3100.github.io/companion.html</code>.",
"modules.companion.page.step2d": "Game on agar.io (browser extension) or inside a frame (for example expanding.land): use the <b>Open companion</b> button in the game. It opens this page and sends the data to that one window only. Keep both open; after reloading the game press the button again.",
"modules.companion.page.step3": "3. OBS",
"modules.companion.page.step3a": "An OBS <b>Browser Source</b> is its own browser: it only receives the data if the game runs in that same browser.",
"modules.companion.page.step3b": "Works everywhere: open the companion link below in a normal browser window with background <b>green</b>, add it to OBS with <b>Window Capture</b> and a <b>Chroma Key</b> filter.",
"modules.companion.page.step3c": "<code>bg=transparent</code> is for a source that shares the browser with the game. <code>demo=1</code> shows sample data to place the widgets.",
"modules.companion.page.privacy": "Privacy",
"modules.companion.page.privacyText": "Stream mode (the eye button in the menu) removes your nick, skin, server address and your teammates' nicks before anything is sent; <b>Hide my country</b> and <b>hide skin URL</b> are respected too. Chat is only sent while its option is on.",
"modules.companion.page.phone": "Phone or another computer",
"modules.companion.page.phoneText": "Not supported yet: pairing two devices needs a WebRTC connection (and a way to exchange the connection offer), which this page does not do. The companion only works next to the game in the same browser.",
"modules.companion.page.build": "Build your overlay link",
